{"assets":["/statement-assets/17e0558ae10fd3a88d4e6338a484bceb68946ebae6ef2b876b653ee51fdbb1c0.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"570","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Simple Game"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One day Misha and Andrew were playing a very simple game. First, each player chooses an integer in the range from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's assume that Misha chose number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":", and Andrew chose number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then, by using a random generator they choose a random integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the range between "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" (any integer from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" is chosen with the same probability), after which the winner is the player, whose number was closer to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":". The boys agreed that if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" are located on the same distance from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":", Misha wins."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Andrew wants to win very much, so he asks you to help him. You know the number selected by Misha, and number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". You need to determine which value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" Andrew must choose, so that the probability of his victory is the highest possible."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"More formally, you need to find such integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ a ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"), that the probability that "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/17e0558ae10fd3a88d4e6338a484bceb68946ebae6ef2b876b653ee51fdbb1c0.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is maximal, where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the equiprobably chosen integer from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" (inclusive)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ m ≤ n ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the range of numbers in the game, and the number selected by Misha respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single number — such value "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", that probability that Andrew wins is the highest. If there are multiple such values, print the minimum of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample test: Andrew wins if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":". The probability that Andrew wins is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 / 3"},{"kind":"text","text":". If Andrew chooses "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a = 3"},{"kind":"text","text":", the probability of winning will be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 / 3"},{"kind":"text","text":". If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", the probability of winning is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample test: Andrew wins if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":". The probability that Andrew wins is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 / 2"},{"kind":"text","text":". For other choices of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" the probability of winning is less."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"570B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/570/problem/B"}